claim.claim-text:
a substrate (SUB) having a plurality of emission regions (EMA);
a first bank (40) on the substrate (SUB) and extending around a periphery of the emission regions (EMA), the first bank (40) comprising a first extension portion (41) extending in a first direction (DR1) and a second extension portion (42) extending in a second direction (DR2) crossing the first direction (DR1);
a plurality of external electrodes (OE) extending in the second direction (DR2) and partially on the second extension portion (42) of the first bank (40);
a plurality of internal electrodes (IE) between the external electrodes (OE) and not overlapping the second extension portion (42) of the first bank (40); and
a plurality of light emitting elements (30) between ones of the external electrodes (OE) and ones of the internal electrodes (IE) or between ones of the internal electrodes (IE).

a substrate (SUB);
a first bank (40) on the substrate (SUB) and comprising a first extension portion (41) extending in a first direction (DR1) and a second extension portion (42) extending in a second direction (DR2) crossing the first direction (DR1);
a first electrode (21) and a second electrode (22) extending in the second direction (DR2) and partially overlapping the second extension portion (42) of the first bank (40), the first electrode (21) and the second electrode (22) being spaced apart from each other in the first direction (DR1);
a third electrode (23) between the first electrode (21) and the second electrode (22) and extending in the second direction (DR2);
a first light emitting element (30) between the first electrode (21) and the third electrode (23);
a second light emitting element (30) between the third electrode (23) and the second electrode (22);
a first contact electrode (26) contacting the first electrode (21) and one end portion of the first light emitting element (30);
a second contact electrode (27) contacting the second electrode (22) and one end portion of the second light emitting element (30); and
a third contact electrode (28) contacting the third electrode (23), another end portion of the first light emitting element (30), and another end portion of the second light emitting element (30).
